Subject: [PATCH 2/3] test(cei): index cei_violation and map it in the
 differential corpus

Registering cei_violation in RuleRegistry::with_default_rules() trips
two registry gates that the original change did not update:

- tests/detector_docs_coverage.rs::index_lists_every_detector requires
  every default detector to be linked from docs/detectors/README.md.
- tests/differential_test.rs::rule_to_code_map_covers_all_default_rules
  requires every default rule in sanctifier_rule_to_code.

Adds the cei_violation row to the detector index and maps both the
rule name and the emitted SANCT_CEI rule_name to SANCT_CEI, matching
the existing cross_contract_call_in_loop entries. No corpus case is
added: the gallery reentrancy fixture's interaction is an event
publish, which cannot call back, so its recorded ground truth is
unchanged.

Refs #336, #310, #325
